# local build outputs (multi-GB qcow2/zst artifacts; keeping them out of git
# also keeps them out of any `git stash -u` during pulls)
build/
build-out-*/
build-failed-*/
build-*.log
*.qcow2
*.qcow2.xz
*.qcow2.zst

# Redox's own prebuilt image and anything unpacked from it. Nothing upstream
# is vendored here -- hooks/host_prepareImage.py fetches it at build time --
# so none of it may ever be committed.
*.img
*.img.zst

# The compiled agent. tools/build-anyvmd.sh produces it from files/anyvmd.rs,
# and it is deliberately NOT committed: it is a binary that would otherwise
# have to be trusted on sight, and rebuilding it is fully pinned (relibc at
# 3da3ff11, redox_syscall =0.5.3, nightly-2024-09-01) so anyone can reproduce
# it byte for byte.
files/anyvmd.bin

# the agent build tree: the relibc clone, the vendored crates and cargo target
build/anyvmd/

# python bytecode caches (hooks/upstream_check.py imports gendata)
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# build.py web-console runtime leftovers
index.html
screen.txt
screen.png
_screenText.txt

# build.py materializes this from enablessh.txt on every run. It is the one
# generated file that deliberately stays at the repo root rather than under
# WORKDIR (build.py:3894 -- several guests' hooks open it by bare name).
# Everything else build.py generates already lands in build/, ignored above:
# the qcow2, the raw img, the pid/port/cmdline state files and the serial log.
enablessh.local
